# Cargo build artefacts. The workspace target/ + per-crate fuzz target/.
# Keep Cargo.lock (binaries — iac, iac-agent, iac-controlplane, iac-trial —
# need a pinned dep tree for reproducible builds).
/target/
/fuzz/target/

# Fuzz outputs. `fuzz/artifacts/` collects libfuzzer crash repros;
# `fuzz/corpus/` is the seed pool. Both grow without bound during a
# campaign; commit only the shrunk repros that get promoted into a
# real test under `crates/*/tests/`.
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/corpus/

# Coverage instrumentation drops these next to the binary.
*.profraw
*.profdata

# Clippy / rustfix leaves `.rs.bk` next to anything it edits when run
# without `--allow-no-vcs`; we gitignore so they don't leak into a
# commit if someone forgets to clean up.
**/*.rs.bk

# Editor / IDE state — different operators use different tools; nobody
# wants a teammate's IDE settings sneaking into the diff.
/.idea/
/.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Runtime state directories that the tool itself creates when run from
# the workspace root (smoke-testing the local CLI). Operators running
# the binaries from a real install path see these under /var/lib/iac/.
/state/
/checkpoints/

# Local agent / controlplane configs that might be dropped at the repo
# root for ad-hoc testing. Production configs live under /etc/iac/;
# never commit a config carrying a real `admin_token` / signing key.
/agent.toml
/server.toml
/iac-trial.toml

# Per-developer scratch — the `temp` file at the repo root is the
# personal session prompt notebook (nothing meaningful for source);
# `/.claude/` is the project-local directory the editor extension
# creates for caching.
/temp
/.claude/

# OS metadata that nothing useful is going to come out of.
Thumbs.db
